    {
      "id": "YRFZ1K759iCTxbEh_6lM-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1329.41015625,
      "y": 360.51953125,
      "width": 2001.818603515625,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1213792037,
      "version": 191,
      "versionNonce": 1954410501,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781830027768,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- When users make Websocket connections to our Chat Server, \nwe'll want to keep track of their connection with a simple in-memory hash map which will map a user id to a websocket connection. This way we know which users are connected and can send them messages.\nTo send a message:\n1. User sends a sendMessage message to the Chat Server.\n2. The Chat Server looks up all participants in the chat via the ChatParticipant table.\n3. The Chat Server looks up the websocket connection for each participant in its internal hash table and sends the message via each connection.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- When users make Websocket connections to our Chat Server, \nwe'll want to keep track of their connection with a simple in-memory hash map which will map a user id to a websocket connection. This way we know which users are connected and can send them messages.\nTo send a message:\n1. User sends a sendMessage message to the Chat Server.\n2. The Chat Server looks up all participants in the chat via the ChatParticipant table.\n3. The Chat Server looks up the websocket connection for each participant in its internal hash table and sends the message via each connection.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "LNsdfnsBBby1xUsGBZ_Vl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1155.966467410003,
      "y": 1203.5634871290677,
      "width": 937.0592651367188,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1624953381,
      "version": 171,
      "versionNonce": 1517713611,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781830665601,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "To solve for the requirement\nSo, to send a message:\n1. Sender sends a sendMessage message to the Chat Server.\n2. The Chat Server looks up all participants in the chat via the ChatParticipant table.\n3. The Chat Server \n(a) writes the message to our Message table and \n(b) creates an entry in our Inbox table for each recipient.\n4. The Chat Server returns a SUCCESS or FAILURE to the sender with the final message id.\n5. The Chat Server looks up the websocket connection \nfor each participant and attempts to deliver the message to each of them via newMessage.\n6. (For connected clients) Upon receipt, \nthe client will send an ack message to the Chat Server \nto indicate they've received the message. \nThe Chat Server will then delete the message from the Inbox table.\n\n-- For clients who aren't connected, we'll keep their messages in the Inbox table for some time. \nLater, when the client decides to connect, we'll:\n1. Look up the user's Inbox and find any undelivered message IDs.\n2. For each message ID, look up the message in the Message table.\n3. Write those messages to the client's connection via the newMessage message.\n4. Upon receipt, the client will send an ack message to the Chat Server \nto indicate they've received the message.\nThe Chat Server will then delete the message from the Inbox table.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "To solve for the requirement\nSo, to send a message:\n1. Sender sends a sendMessage message to the Chat Server.\n2. The Chat Server looks up all participants in the chat via the ChatParticipant table.\n3. The Chat Server \n(a) writes the message to our Message table and \n(b) creates an entry in our Inbox table for each recipient.\n4. The Chat Server returns a SUCCESS or FAILURE to the sender with the final message id.\n5. The Chat Server looks up the websocket connection \nfor each participant and attempts to deliver the message to each of them via newMessage.\n6. (For connected clients) Upon receipt, \nthe client will send an ack message to the Chat Server \nto indicate they've received the message. \nThe Chat Server will then delete the message from the Inbox table.\n\n-- For clients who aren't connected, we'll keep their messages in the Inbox table for some time. \nLater, when the client decides to connect, we'll:\n1. Look up the user's Inbox and find any undelivered message IDs.\n2. For each message ID, look up the message in the Message table.\n3. Write those messages to the client's connection via the newMessage message.\n4. Upon receipt, the client will send an ack message to the Chat Server \nto indicate they've received the message.\nThe Chat Server will then delete the message from the Inbox table.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
