    {
      "id": "xTTRkiOENYDwdWQuSJ-Hp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1675.5498454525296,
      "y": 2007.8621069604305,
      "width": 668.53955078125,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b65",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1967849349,
      "version": 17,
      "versionNonce": 1578685829,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781831063489,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- To do this we'll need to keep a central registry of\n how many Chat Servers we have, their addresses, \nand the which segments of a consistent hash space they own. \nWe might use a service like ZooKeeper or Etcd to do this.\nWhen a request comes in, we'll connect them to the Chat Server \nthey are assigned to based on their user id. \n-- When a new event is created, \nChat Servers will connect directly with the Chat Server that \"owns\" \nthat user id, then call an API which delivers \na notification the connected user (if they're connected).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- To do this we'll need to keep a central registry of\n how many Chat Servers we have, their addresses, \nand the which segments of a consistent hash space they own. \nWe might use a service like ZooKeeper or Etcd to do this.\nWhen a request comes in, we'll connect them to the Chat Server \nthey are assigned to based on their user id. \n-- When a new event is created, \nChat Servers will connect directly with the Chat Server that \"owns\" \nthat user id, then call an API which delivers \na notification the connected user (if they're connected).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
